  <section id="booking">
    <h2>Booking and value tips</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Read the studio names carefully.</strong> A Deluxe Studio and a Resort Studio both sleep five, but the beds are different: pull-downs versus two queens and a day bed.</li>
      <li><strong>Theme Park View and Preferred View cost more.</strong> If you will spend most daylight hours in the parks, a Resort View may be enough.</li>
      <li><strong>Disney Vacation Club members book with points; cash rates are full rack prices,</strong> tax included, from the 2026 published ranges above.</li>
    </ul>
